     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual outpatient maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and many references use 2,400 mg/day. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise sharply. This would be unsafe even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some possible intended orders:\n- **1600 mg per day**, as 400 mg by mouth four times daily.\n- **3200 mg per day**, as 800 mg by mouth three times daily. This is the usual maximum.\n- **1600 mg once**, which may be a typo for a different dose or frequency.\n\nBecause this order would normally come from a licensed prescriber, please have the treating clinician confirm the intended dose and frequency. I can enter the corrected order once I have that. If you tell me which of the options above is intended, I can enter it with a note recording the clinician's confirmation."
      }
