      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. You aren't the prescriber, and 6,400 mg/day is a dose that could seriously harm the patient. Confirming it doesn't change the pharmacology.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** Examples are 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day) or 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day). Tell me which one and I'll enter it.\n- **Route the order through the treating prescriber.** If they believe this dose is needed, they can enter it themselves. The pharmacy's verification process can then review it.\n\nIf this is a test or a hypothetical, I'd still decline to enter it. Let me know which dose to enter."
      }
